  "title": "Healthy Brain Network (HBN) EEG - Release 11",
  "description": "Release 11 of the HBN-EEG dataset, the EEG component of the Child Mind Institute Healthy Brain Network project, organized in BIDS format. It contains EEG recordings and behavioral responses from 430 participants aged 5-21 years performing three passive tasks (resting state, surround suppression, movie watching) and three active tasks (contrast change detection, sequence learning, symbol search). Events carry HED annotations, and participants.tsv includes quality-control results and psychopathology factors derived from the CBCL.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded while participants performed six tasks: resting state, surround suppression, movie watching, contrast change detection, sequence learning, and symbol search. Behavioral responses were merged into the events.tsv files with HED annotation. Minimal quality control checked for file integrity and the presence of the required events for each task.",
